    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_63f6c8f6a0a1deb0b2f36dcdcee99dae5e265f434820ae76864e96538494b537",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The primon gas realizes unique factorization as occupation-number bookkeeping. A prime p labels a one-particle level with energy proportional to log p; bosonic multiplicities are prime exponents, so each many-body state corresponds uniquely to an integer n and has total energy proportional to log n. Summing its Boltzmann weights is therefore the zeta Dirichlet series, whose pole becomes a Hagedorn divergence. Fermionic exclusion changes allowed exponents to zero or one and correspondingly changes the Euler factors and partition-function ratio.",
