    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1ef4fb3b3c4cb2df79a506567fed195b38070b835909bd56bd662b46e97a74df",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source repeatedly obtains physical thresholds by composing a zeta-type analytic object with a representation-specific control parameter. Dimension sends the Riemann-zeta pole to the two-dimensional Bose-gas obstruction, inverse temperature sends the same pole to the primon-gas Hagedorn threshold, and Mellin inversion orders leading and subleading zeta poles into bulk and finite-size effects; a transform denominator likewise turns admissibility of phonon density into a zero-free condition. The Epstein-zeta counterexamples show why these translations are informative only when the controlling map and observable constraint are specified: lattice provenance, continuation, and functional symmetry alone do not transfer a critical-line property.",
