    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6b42568b500b3bbc0d2f175a8951f53fabda14c2eecf207b6dd2bf6db9a3b417",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source's zeta density and dynamical trace formulas share a two-layer architecture: a smooth spectral count plus oscillations indexed by primitive objects and repetitions. Reading the prime-power expansion with the classical and quantum trace mechanisms identifies primes as candidate primitive-orbit labels, repetitions r as orbit repeats, and log p as period/action data; the later dictionary then turns the simultaneous matches into conditional constraints on a hypothetical Riemann dynamics. Zero statistics thereby specify tests for candidate orbit dynamics without constructing that dynamics.",
